## Implementation Standards

When using a referenced UI pattern:

- Prefer composition over duplication.
- Keep components small and readable.
- Use existing project primitives whenever possible.
- Use semantic HTML.
- Preserve keyboard navigation.
- Preserve focus states.
- Preserve accessible labels.
- Ensure mobile responsiveness.
- Avoid unreadable contrast.
- Avoid animation that harms usability.
- Avoid unnecessary dependency additions.
- Avoid introducing a new design system unless explicitly requested.

## Do Not

- Do not paste paid component code unless the license is confirmed.
- Do not introduce a new UI framework without explicit approval.
- Do not introduce a new CSS architecture unless it aligns with the current project.
- Do not ship decorative motion that reduces readability.
- Do not create duplicate components when an existing primitive can be extended.
- Do not hardcode colors if project tokens exist.
- Do not ignore accessibility requirements.
- Do not use a design pattern that conflicts with the product’s tone, purpose, or user context.